---A `SeqType` config contains the playback data properties associated with a given animation's frames.
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.Seq` table:
---
---Info: A `SeqType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot, however,
---be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Information available within an `SeqType` includes:
---@class SeqType
---@field id integer (Read-only) The ID of this config type.
---@field configName string (Read-only) The name of this config, i.e. `"ARDRAGON_DRAGON_BASIC_ICE_ATTACK"`.
---@field typeName string (Read-only) The type of this config. Will always be `"Seq"`.
---@field preAnimMove PreAnimMove (Read-only) Behaviour of the animation if the entity is moving when it starts playing.
---@field postAnimMove PostAnimMove (Read-only) Behaviour of the animation if the entity is wants to move after it starts playing.
---@field length integer (Read-only) Number of client ticks the associated animation will run for.
---@field loop integer (Read-only) How many more loops the animation will run for.
---@field priority integer (Read-only) Priority of the animation. Higher is more important.
---@field replaceHeldLeft ObjType? (Read-only) Object of what to replace the entity's left hand is holding with.
---@field replaceHeldRight ObjType? (Read-only) Object of what to replace the entity's right hand is holding with.
---@field maxLoop integer (Read-only) Maximum number of loops this animation can run for.
---@field animDuplicateBehaviour AnimationDuplicateBehaviour (Read-only) Determines what happens if the same animation is requested to be played while it is already being played.
local SeqType = {}

